<title>UK: J.P. Morgan joins South Africa Futures Exchange.</title>
<headline>J.P. Morgan joins South Africa Futures Exchange.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>J.P. Morgan has become a member of the South African Futures Exchange (SAFEX), the bank said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Membership of SAFEX gives us the capacity to provide a fuller range of services to our South African clients,&quot; said Ronald Gault, head of J.P. Morgan's South Africa office in the statement.</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan has had an office in South Africa since October 1996, the statement said.</p>
<p>Founded in 1990, SAFEX turnover in 1996 grew by 26 percent to 9.3 million contracts, mainly in equity index futures and options, it noted.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
